(Bug #54's controls: every element read whose type the compiler can prove
 MATCHES its destination still compiles and still answers correctly, and
 every read it cannot prove is still allowed through. The mismatches
 themselves live in the compile_fail corpus, cases 099-104.)

(A matching read - the shape the fix must not touch.)
a list called counts is [1, 2].
a number called 'first count' is element 1 of counts.
Print 'first count'.

a list called names is ["alpha", "beta"].
a text called 'second name' is element 2 of names.
Print 'second name'.

(The same reads through 's first / 's last.)
Print counts's first.
Print names's last.

(A mixed list yields a value, which takes an element of any type.)
a list called oddments is [7, "seven"].
a value called 'counted half' is element 1 of oddments.
a value called 'worded half' is element 2 of oddments.
Print 'counted half'.
Print 'worded half'.

(An append of another type widens the list, so no element type is provable
 any more and a read of the appended element is allowed through - proving
 the check is not a stale reading of the declaration alone.)
a list called grown is [1, 2].
Append "three" to grown.
a text called third is element 3 of grown.
Print third.

(A byte is a number wherever it comes from.)
a buffer called raw is 16 bytes in size.
raw is "hi".
a number called 'letter code' is byte 1 of raw.
Print 'letter code'.

(A map's proven value type matches its destination.)
a map called ages is {"bo": 42}.
a number called 'bo age' is ages's "bo".
Print 'bo age'.

(A loop variable over a proven list carries the element type: arithmetic on
 it still works, and so does printing and copying a text element.)
a number called 'counted up' is 0.
For each part in counts,
    'counted up' is 'counted up' add part.
Print 'counted up'.

a text called 'last name' is "".
For each word in names,
    'last name' is word.
Print 'last name'.

(An element of a proven number list is still a number in arithmetic.)
a number called total is 0.
total is total add element 2 of counts.
Print total.
